  "doc.title": "How Memory Talks to the CPU · a long essay you can play with",
  "doc.desc": "A DDR5-6400 CL32 module has a bigger latency number than DDR4: is it faster? What happens inside the module when the CPU asks for one byte? Why does memory still use a wide set of parallel wires? Ten models: how much time refresh takes, which row an address lands in, a cycle-by-cycle DRAM command simulator, CL in cycles and nanoseconds, bandwidth against row hits, bank groups, fly-by routing and training, on-die and side-band ECC, PAM3, and row hammer with its defences.",
